@3. The modules (8)
=STRCASE.INC.BL -- case, in place
.
.Routines, arguments and examples: SEC 4.8.
.
.  in
.      STRCASE.PTR -- GP.STRPTR of the string
.      STRCASE.MODE -- STRCASE.UPPER or STRCASE.LOWER
.
.  out
.      the string itself, rewritten in place
.
.  verbs
.      STR.UCASE STR.LCASE -- a string in, a cased copy back, through
.        STRCASE.S$
.
.  internal
.      STRCASE.ADDR% STRCASE.OP% STRCASE.S$
.
.  constants
.      STRCASE.UPPER STRCASE.LOWER
.
.STR.UCASE and STR.LCASE are the two STR. names this file owns. The rest of
.STR. is STRINGS.INC.BL's, and the two verbs are named for the module they
.are to move into.
.
.#SYMFILE again. Do not write #AUTONUM in a program that includes this -- it
.sets the STEP, and only the default 1 survives.
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  FORM.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.
=SEE ALSO
.
